{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the leaders.</b> For when they went out from Egypt, every man plundered according to his standing, and behold it was a great thing that oil for the lamp was found in the leaders' hands after many months since they had left Egypt. And afterward he gathered all men and women together and returned to speak of the women whose hearts moved them to act. And he mentioned the leader first, that all of them would be subject to his authority, for there is none among them as wise as he."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:40.437994429Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}